        "original_id": "912b21ca-6123-598f-a7d8-a4102299c048",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: David Thewlis, Patty Jenkins, Allan Heinberg, Zack Snyder, Jason Fuchs, Gal Gadot, Chris Pine, Robin Wright, Danny Huston, Connie Nielsen, Elena Anaya, Sia, Labrinth\n- Works: James and the Giant Peach, The Miracle Maker, Anomalisa, Fargo, Wonder Woman, To Be Human\n- Organizations: FX\n- Concepts: anthology format, soundtrack\n\nFacts:\n- David Thewlis did voice work in the films \"James and the Giant Peach\" (1996), \"The Miracle Maker\" (2000), and \"Anomalisa\" (2015).\n- Fargo premiered on April 15, 2014, on FX.\n- Fargo follows an anthology format, with each season set in a different era and featuring a different story and mostly new characters and cast, although there is minor overlap.\n- Wonder Woman is directed by Patty Jenkins, with a screenplay by Allan Heinberg from a story by Allan Heinberg, Zack Snyder, and Jason Fuchs.\n- Wonder Woman stars Gal Gadot, Chris Pine, Robin Wright, Danny Huston, David Thewlis, Connie Nielsen, and Elena Anaya.\n- \"To Be Human\" is a song recorded by Australian singer Sia featuring English singer Labrinth for the soundtrack to the 2017 superhero film Wonder Woman.",
